## <host-b> — 132,000-entry host
  Still executing at 1021s, 100% CPU, output buffered (AIDE writes at the end).
  The 900s ssh session timeout fired first; the remote process survived it.
  -> KNOWN_ISSUES.md#the-runner-s-fixed-900-second-command-ti_b1115836
  -> DEFAULT_TIMEOUT raised 900 -> 3600, per-host override, timeout given its
     own verdict so a slow check never again reads as an unreachable host.

## What this run establishes about the TOOL
  1. --config fix works: AIDE executed and returned a real verdict (exit 7),
     where the sweep of the same day returned exit 17 having checked nothing.
  2. 900s was too short, measured rather than guessed this time.
  3. The classifier's bitmask decode was correct on real output: exit 7
     decomposes to new + removed + changed, and all three were present.
